for(key) to obtain the hook for a specific key (creating it on demand) and then tap on it as usual: The owner of the HookMap uses get(key) to look up an existing hook without creating one. This is typically preferred on the calling side so that keys no plugin cares about are never materialized:

A HookMap can also be intercepted. intercept({ factory }) wraps the factory so you can customize or replace the hook returned for each new key.

